cores zero fans but qualifies because it's the default 8-point minimum. However, Chicken Hand only counts when you have no other scoring elements. But let\u2019s check what little value I might have:  \n    - **All Chows**: 2 points  \n    - Possibly **One Voided Suit**: I have W (Characters), T (Bamboo), B (Dots) \u2014 all three suits present \u2192 \u274c  \n    - **No Honors**: I don\u2019t have any honor tiles in hand or melds \u2192 actually true! My melds are all suited, hand has no honors \u2192 \u2705 No Honors (1 point)  \n    - So currently, I could have: All Chows (2) + No Honors (1) = 3 points. Not enough. Need at least 8.\n\nBut wait \u2014 **Chicken Hand** (8 points) applies specifically when your hand would otherwise score zero fans *but* you complete a legal win. However, per MCR rules, **Chicken Hand is only valid when no other pattern applies**, including even 1-fan patterns like All Chows or No Honors. Since I have All Chows (2 fans), Chicken Hand is blocked.\n\nSo I must improve my fan count.\n\nAlternative idea: Can I form a **pair** from existing tiles?\n\nCurrent hand: W8, W9, W9, T1, T9\n\nIf I draw a tile later to make a pair, e.g., W8+W8, but I only have one W8 now.\n\nBut perhaps target **Pung of Terminals or Honors** \u2014 each such pung gives 1 point. Currently, none of my melds are terminal/honor based except [B7,B8,B9] \u2014 these are terminals (7,8,9). So that counts as one **Pung of Terminals or Honors** (1 point). Similarly, [T2,T3,T4] is not terminal. [W3,W4,W5] is not. So only one such pung.\n\nStill low.\n\nWait \u2014 reconsider **Lower Four / Upper Four / Tiles groupings**:\n\n- [B7,B8,B9] is Upper Tiles (7\u20139), but others aren't.  \n- Not helpful.\n\nBack to move evaluation:\n\nAvailable discards: Play W9, Play W8, Play T1, Play T9\n\nLet\u2019s analyze implications:\n\n- **Discard W8**: Leaves W9\u00d72, T1, T9. Keeps chance to draw/claim W9 for pung (possible Pung of Terminals). Also keeps symmetry. But W8 is part of 