value.\n\nSo: **Keep W9 pair** for potential pair-based waits.\n\nAlso consider safety: who might win on what?\n\n- Any player completing a pair? Hard to say.\n- But **discard safety priority**.\n\nNow check: which of these tiles could complete a *winning hand*?\n\n- B2: Could complete 1-2-3 or 2-3-4. But B1 is all gone (Peng + discards), so 1-2-3 impossible. Only 2-3-4 possible. Next player already has B2-B3-B4 \u2014 so they don\u2019t need more. Others haven't shown B3/B4. So B2 likely safe.\n\n- W8: W6-W7-W8 already melded by next player. Unlikely anyone else needs it. Safe.\n\n- W9: Could complete 7-8-9. Next player already completed W6-W7-W8 \u2192 they don\u2019t have W9. Did they discard W9? No \u2014 they discarded W1, W7, etc., but not W9. Could they be waiting on W9? Unlikely. Across player discarded W8 \u2014 suggests weak W hand. Probably safe.\n\n- T9: Across player discarded T9 twice \u2014 suggests they are getting rid of them. So likely safe. But T9 is terminal \u2014 higher chance of being part of a pattern like Outside Hand, etc.\n\nBut here\u2019s a better idea: **maximize fan value**.\n\nCurrent hand: three chows, all mixed suits. If I can form a fourth chow and get a pair, I can win with **All Chows** (2 points), plus possibly **No Honors** (1 point), **One Voided Suit**? I have all three suits \u2014 no. One Voided Suit requires missing one suit entirely \u2014 I have all three \u2192 no.\n\nWait: my melds: [B7,B8,B9] (Bamboo), [W3,W4,W5] (Character), [T2,T3,T4] (Dot) \u2014 so all three suits present. Cannot get One Voided Suit.\n\nBut if I keep a pair and win with All Chows, that\u2019s 2 points. Need at least 8 total.\n\nCurrently, what patterns do I have?\n\n- All Chows: 2 points\n- No Honors: 1 point (if pair is not honor)\n- Self Drawn: 1 point (if I draw the winning tile)\n- Mixed Double Chow: ? Do I have two identical chows? No \u2014 all different.\n- Short Straight? W3-4-5 and possibly W4-5-6? No.\n- Mixed Shifted Chows? T2-3-4 and W